     x86/boot: Clear BSS-like regions in the kernel ELF parser
     =

     The ELF spec describes PT_LOAD segments thus:
     =

       If the segment's memory size (p_memsz) is larger than the file
       size (p_filesz), the "extra" bytes are defined to hold the value 0
       and to follow the segment's initialized area.  The file size may
       not be larger than the memory size.
     =

     Historically, the kernel's ELF decompressor left garbage in the
     region between p_filesz and p_memsz.  Fix it.
     =

     This causes BSS to be automatically cleared when the kernel is
     loaded.  It will also make other BSS-like (SHT_NOBITS) ELF sections
     work correctly.
     =

     This lets us opt in to generic ROBSS support.
     =

     Fixes: 099e1377269a ("x86: use ELF format in compressed images.")
     Signed-off-by: Andy Lutomirski <luto@kernel.org>
     =

